.env
.venv
_retired/
__pycache__/

# Generated books, cached per character/level/party/DB version/scenario. User data,
# like data/, and never a build artefact.
.cache/

# Root-level Node leftovers from the retired browser-only RAG plan. Scoped to the root
# with a leading slash so the front end, which has to commit its lockfile, still can.
/node_modules/
/package-lock.json

# A fetched third-party plugin checkout (see DnD-Character-Sheet-Helper.PROVENANCE.md,
# which sits outside this directory for the reason below). Ignored rather than committed
# so the repo does not redistribute it, and ignored rather than left untracked so
# `git add -A` cannot turn the nested `.git` into a gitlink - which commits a commit
# pointer and no content, leaving a fresh clone with an empty directory.
#
# The whole directory, and not `/*` with a `!` negation for the provenance file: git will
# not descend into an ignored directory, so a negation *inside* it does not apply to the
# directory itself and `git add -A` still stages the gitlink. Verified both ways.
context/DnD-Character-Sheet-Helper/
context/DnD-Character-Sheet-Helper
